WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.054 --> 00:00:12.509
"Wow, this store is huge!" Ally thought as she entered Everything Mart and grabbed a shopping basket.

2
00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:18.174
"It looks like they really do sell everything here!"

3
00:00:18.175 --> 00:00:21.947
Ally headed first for the hardware department.

4
00:00:21.948 --> 00:00:28.795
"Hmm . . . I see hammers, nails, plywood, and paint, but no fuel cells or spaceship parts.

5
00:00:28.796 --> 00:00:31.032
I guess I'd better ask for some help."

6
00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:35.715
Ally spotted a teenager stocking the shelves.

7
00:00:35.716 --> 00:00:41.716
"Excuse me," she said. "Can you please tell me where I can find beta-booster coils?"

8
00:00:41.717 --> 00:00:44.634
"Huh?" The boy scratched his chin.

9
00:00:44.635 --> 00:00:49.680
"I never heard of those, but I just started working here. Let me check the inventory."

10
00:00:49.681 --> 00:00:52.689
He pulled out a handheld device and did a quick search.

11
00:00:52.690 --> 00:01:00.380
"Found it!" he exclaimed. "You're in the wrong department. Beta boosters are in aisle 34."

12
00:01:00.381 --> 00:01:02.854
"Phew!" Ally thought in relief.

13
00:01:02.855 --> 00:01:08.696
"I was worried they might not have what I need." She thanked the worker and headed over.

14
00:01:08.697 --> 00:01:18.075
In aisle 34 Ally was thrilled to see that the shelves were stocked with all kinds of space items like lasers, comm devices, and even spacesuits and helmets.

15
00:01:18.076 --> 00:01:21.610
"This is more like it!" she said.

16
00:01:21.611 --> 00:01:25.860
Ally walked up and down the aisle, searching for the things she needed.

17
00:01:25.861 --> 00:01:28.472
"Where are they?" she murmured.

18
00:01:28.473 --> 00:01:37.504
Just as disappointment began to creep in, she spotted a crowded bottom shelf marked "Clearance Items."

19
00:01:37.505 --> 00:01:42.447
"What a strange way to store parts," she thought, rummaging through the stuff on the shelf.

20
00:01:42.448 --> 00:01:45.881
"But humans certainly do have a lot of strange habits."

21
00:01:45.882 --> 00:01:48.368
Ally carefully began pulling things off the shelf.

22
00:01:48.369 --> 00:01:52.890
They were mostly broken comm devices and a few banged-up helmets.

23
00:01:52.891 --> 00:02:00.230
But then she spotted a gleaming silver canister marked "Fuel."

24
00:02:00.231 --> 00:02:06.499
"Success!" she cried as she placed the fuel cell into her shopping basket. "Finally!"

25
00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:12.157
Ally kept looking through the items on the shelf, but she didn't see anything else that she needed.

26
00:02:12.158 --> 00:02:14.836
"At least I've got some fuel," she thought.

27
00:02:14.837 --> 00:02:20.596
"When I'm back in the pod, I'll check with Alpha, but this fuel cell could probably get us halfway home."

28
00:02:20.597 --> 00:02:25.507
Ally was about to go to the checkout line when she spotted something familiar on a nearby shelf.

29
00:02:25.508 --> 00:02:28.291
It was a small replica of her escape pod.

30
00:02:28.292 --> 00:02:35.762
Amazed, Ally pulled it off the shelf. "How could this be?"

31
00:02:35.763 --> 00:02:39.629
She blinked when she finally realized what she was holding.

32
00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:45.114
She groaned. "It's just a toy!"

33
00:02:45.115 --> 00:02:48.880
She yanked the fuel cell out of the shopping basket and looked at it more closely.

34
00:02:48.881 --> 00:02:53.813
"And so is this! These are all toys!" Her shoulders slumped.

35
00:02:53.814 --> 00:02:57.449
"I thought they had everything here!"

36
00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:01.547
A store manager walked by.

37
00:03:01.548 --> 00:03:05.613
"Is there something I can help you with, miss?" he asked.

38
00:03:05.614 --> 00:03:11.285
"Yes, please!" Ally said. "I'm looking for beta-booster coils and fuel cells.

39
00:03:11.286 --> 00:03:15.612
A clerk told me they'd be in aisle 34, but they're not here."

40
00:03:15.613 --> 00:03:20.320
"I apologize for the inconvenience," the manager said.

41
00:03:20.321 --> 00:03:25.263
"We just hired some new staff, and they're still learning about the store."

42
00:03:25.264 --> 00:03:28.510
He lowered his voice and chuckled.

43
00:03:28.511 --> 00:03:34.539
"Everyone knows that beta boosters are in the health food section!"

44
00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:38.860
Ally frowned. "Hmm. That doesn't sound quite right.

45
00:03:38.861 --> 00:03:44.116
Beta-booster coils aren't a healthy food. They're parts for a spaceship engine."

46
00:03:44.117 --> 00:03:47.731
"Oh." The manager gave her an odd look.

47
00:03:47.732 --> 00:03:54.707
"Then I have another suggestion—try the Sandville UFO Museum gift shop."

48
00:03:54.708 --> 00:03:57.440
"Argh!" Ally thought in frustration.

49
00:03:57.441 --> 00:04:02.855
"I'm just going in circles!" She glanced up at a clock.

50
00:04:02.856 --> 00:04:11.862
"And now I've run out of time." She had to get to the diner to start training Barry.

51
00:04:11.863 --> 00:04:16.113
Barry followed Ally around for the first part of her shift as she waited on customers.

52
00:04:16.114 --> 00:04:19.791
After a couple of hours, she handed him his own apron and pad.

53
00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:24.256
"I think you're ready to serve customers on your own now," she said.

54
00:04:24.257 --> 00:04:26.567
"Why don't you take table five's order?"

55
00:04:26.568 --> 00:04:28.437
"Okay!"

56
00:04:28.438 --> 00:04:36.381
While Barry took care of the customers, Ally waited for Ray to finish cooking some Beta Burganas for one of her tables.

57
00:04:36.382 --> 00:04:39.528
"How did Flo do this morning?" she asked.

58
00:04:39.529 --> 00:04:44.595
"Fine." Ray sighed. "The customers really like her."

59
00:04:44.596 --> 00:04:49.037
"That's wonderful!" Ally said. "Isn't it?"

60
00:04:49.038 --> 00:04:53.676
"Yeah, it is." Ray smiled as he put down the burgers for Ally's table.

61
00:04:53.677 --> 00:04:56.147
But Ally sensed that something was wrong.

62
00:04:56.148 --> 00:05:00.807
So far she'd resisted trying to read Ray's thoughts, but now she couldn't stop herself.

63
00:05:00.808 --> 00:05:06.237
And she quickly read something sad—Ray was feeling lonely.

64
00:05:06.238 --> 00:05:12.126
"The poor guy," Ally thought. "Work isn't everything."

65
00:05:12.127 --> 00:05:15.171
She served the burgers to her customers, still thinking about Ray.

66
00:05:15.172 --> 00:05:19.190
She had to come up with some ways to help him, like a true Astralian.

67
00:05:19.191 --> 00:05:28.938
"By the time I leave," Ally vowed, "he's going to be happier!"

